<title>FRANCE: Algeria to allow foreign currency exchange offices.</title>
<headline>Algeria to allow foreign currency exchange offices.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's Central Bank will allow private sector operators to open money changing shops, the official Algerian new agency APS said on Monday.</p>
<p>A Central Bank statement carried by APS said the decision was designed to facilitate exchange operations and improve the quality of service to customers. It did not spell out requirements and regulations governing the exchange offices.</p>
<p>Foreign exchange dealings in Algeria have been restricted to state-controlled banks.</p>
</text>
